    37	handling, cofactor equation variant, and negative test vectors for each*. Two of those fields name concepts of
    38	Ed25519-style curves, which A1 used as its example (`:136`). V1 later registered OpenPGP P-256 and then, on
    39	2026-10-16, the hybrid ML-DSA-65 + P-256 (`formal/p8/HYBRID-REGISTRATION-RECORD.md`). Neither registration re-read the
    40	checklist.
    41	
    42	For ML-DSA, the two curve fields have no referent. The other four fields still apply in full. So the checklist
    43	names nothing specific to ML-DSA's own verification pitfalls: it **demands too little**. Nothing had been accepted
    44	on it. The assumption half was open (`formal/PROPERTIES.md:37`) and due after the freeze
    45	(`formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:81`).
    46	
    47	The method's defect: **a registered decision can change what an earlier registered sentence refers to, and nothing
