   131	## A11.4 Dependency duty for registered decisions
   132	
   133	When a registered decision changes a parameter (an algorithm, a custody form, a channel, a horizon, a scope, a key),
   134	the owner sweeps the registered texts for sentences whose referent the change alters. Each one is recorded as
   135	amended, superseded, still fitting or open, before the decision's change is treated as complete. An owner decision
   136	that touches a registered parameter is checked against those texts before it is recorded.
   137	
   138	## A11.5 Results of the first sweep (2026-10-28)
   139	
   140	The sweep covered the original, Amendments 1–10, the freeze, the tracker and the author-rulings files
   141	(`docs/reviews/stale-dependencies/SWEEP-2026-10-28.md`). The owner checked each finding against its source. The
   142	review added item 3. The sweep did not read the rest of the frozen specification or the hybrid supplement
   143	(`SWEEP-2026-10-28.md:3-4`, `:20-21`). The Levadura panel read them. Its findings are §A11.3 rows 1, 2, 4–6, 8 and
   144	10–14, §A11.6 and §A11.7.
   145	
   146	**Scope from now on.** Every sweep under §A11.4 reads the frozen specification object in full (`spec.bin`: A9, A10,
   147	PROOF, V1-PROFILE, ENCODING-V1 and the hybrid supplement; `formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:16`), as well as the
   148	original, every amendment, the freeze record, the tracker and the author-rulings files.
   149	
   150	1. **H3 (`phase-0-prereg.md:232-248`): not amended.** H3 is a hypothesis with a stated falsifier. Its examples are
   151	   AWS-based, but they do not restrict it to AWS. It is measured over the whole deployed system, every provider
   152	   included. A measurement protocol is recorded before measurement. It covers retained resources (including the
   153	   compliance-locked trail bucket), defines the demonstration and idle periods, and reports the three numbers
   154	   separately. A slot-2 signer and an issuer poller that run through the operating window conflict with "idle
   155	   compute exactly $0". If that or another number fails, H3 is reported as falsified. The operating window is not
   156	   redefined as a demonstration to avoid this.
   157	2. **The slot-2 enforcement boundary: for the author's ruling.** A9.6 requires the final custody implementation to
   158	   be deadline-qualified (`phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:389-392`). The frozen record keeps "the selected,
   159	   deadline-qualified custody implementation" (`270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1024-1025`). It describes it through
   160	   `prototype/policy-signer/` (:1033-1037), which met the deadline on 2026-10-14 (:1038-1040; §14.2 item 5,
   161	   :1429-1435). That qualification stands as historical evidence.
   162	
   163	   Production cannot run the prototype. Instrument code under `prototype/` stays instrument code, and service code
   164	   that ports it must earn its own evidence on its own bytes (`formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:62-64`). Nothing an
   165	   instrument produces discharges an obligation (A9:198-200). The E9 ruling R5b (`docs/reviews/e9-packet/AUTHOR-RULINGS.md:54`)
   166	   allows porting instrument code with evidence earned on the resulting bytes. It does not address A9.6's
   167	   deadline-qualified custody, so it does not settle this question. The registered texts do not say whether a
   168	   post-deadline port counts as "the selected, deadline-qualified custody implementation". Each reading keeps a
   169	   different registered text, so the author has to choose.
   170	
   171	   > **AUTHOR RULING: PENDING.**
   172	   >
   173	   > **Option 1: the custody implementation is the custody option and boundary (port permitted; keeps the hybrid).**
   174	   > A signed row says the A9.6 deadline qualification (A9:389-392; `270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1024-1025`,
   175	   > `:1429-1435`) attaches to the selected custody option and boundary: GCP Cloud KMS HSM, P-256, non-exportable,
   176	   > behind a queue-pulling policy signer with the A9.6 checks (A9:382-388). The 2026-10-14 instrument run evidenced
